The code above is a series of unit tests for the ArrayList collection type using Pex in a Visual Studio 2012 environment. 

This code tests the Add, Remove, Insert, Set, Get, Contains, IndexOf, and LastIndexOf methods in the ArrayList. For each method, we capture all the state/preconditions/postconditions. Then we run the operation and capture the new state to ensure the operation has executed correctly.

There may be a mistake I didn't account for, as it seems there was not enough detail in the code. The assertions seem to indicate that if the method returns -1 (which means the item was not found), then the size of a collection should be -1. 

